1
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:42,000
A New Evil Awakens.

2
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:18,000
The Mummy: Tomb of the Dragon Emperor is a adventure,
action, fantasy film directed by Rob Cohen.

3
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Archaeologist Rick O'Connell travels to China, pitting him against an emperor from the
2,000-year-old Han dynasty who's returned from the dead to pursue a quest for world domination.

4
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
This time, O'Connell enlists the help of his wife and son to quash the
so-called 'Dragon Emperor' and his abuse of supernatural power.

5
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Rick O'Connell, played by Brendan Fraser.

6
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Evelyn O'Connell, played by Maria Bello.

7
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:18,000
Jonathan Carnahan, played by John Hannah.

8
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Alex O'Connell, played by Luke Ford.

9
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
Lin, played by Isabella Leong Lok-Sze.

10
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Han, played by Jet Li.

11
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
The Mummy: Tomb of the Dragon Emperor is a 2008 American action adventure fantasy film directed by Rob Cohen, written by Alfred Gough and
Miles Millar, and produced by Stephen Sommers (director of the first two films), Bob Ducsay, Sean Daniel, and James Jacks.

12
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film is set in China rather than Egypt and
focuses on the Terracotta Army's origins.

13
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
It is the third installment in The Mummy series.

14
01:18:24,000 --> 01:18:30,000
It stars Brendan Fraser, Jet Li, Maria Bello (replacing Rachel Weisz, who played Evelyn in
the first two films), John Hannah, Luke Ford, Anthony Wong, and Michelle Yeoh.

15
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The Mummy: Tomb of the Dragon Emperor premiered in Moscow on July 24, 2008,
and was released in the United States on August 1, 2008.

16
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
The film was a commercial success, grossing $405.8 million worldwide, though it was the
lowest-grossing film in the trilogy and received generally negative reviews from critics.

17
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
Universal Pictures rebooted the Mummy franchise with a 2017 reboot film, in an
attempt to start a cinematic universe under the name Dark Universe.

18
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
A sequel is in development.

19
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:30,000
The film explores themes of china, sword, pyramid, mummy, yeti.
